This task is very challenging to machines and still a very active area of research.

\paragraph{Retrieval-based QA.}
The first approach to open-domain QA was to formulate the task as a retrieval problem \cite{voorhees1999trec}. In such a setup, the goal is to answer a question by retrieving a document that contains the correct answer. This setup allows a very efficient search over a large collection of documents, but has the obvious problem of having to decide on what documents are in the collection and thus restricts the set of possible answers.
